50
00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:56.920
True. Not only is it popular, but it's also creating new careers.

51
00:02:58.217 --> 00:03:01.586
Grammar focus: Inversion after negative adverbials.

52
00:03:01.886 --> 00:03:06.138
In formal English, we can start a sentence with a negative adverb for emphasis.

53
00:03:06.438 --> 00:03:09.680
After never, rarely or not only, use question word order.

54
00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:13.466
For example: Never have I seen such a fast runner.

55
00:03:13.766 --> 00:03:17.971
After these negative words at the start of a sentence, use question word order.

56
00:03:18.983 --> 00:03:21.868
Now read and listen. The Changing Face of Sport.

57
00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:26.606
Professional sport today depends heavily on sponsorship and television money.

58
00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:31.449
Never before have athletes earned so much, or faced so much pressure.

59
00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:36.897
Scandals like doping and match-fixing have damaged trust in some sports.

60
00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:42.737
At the same time, esports and new fan culture are attracting young audiences.

61
00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:48.534
Not only is sport entertainment, but it also shapes national identity.

62
00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.154
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:52.454 --> 00:03:55.429
Using illegal drugs to improve performance is blank.

64
00:03:55.729 --> 00:03:59.777
A, doping. B, sponsorship. C, esports.

65
00:04:03.783 --> 00:04:05.307
The answer is A: doping.

66
00:04:06.817 --> 00:04:08.700
Never blank such a beautiful goal.

67
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.468
A, I have seen. B, have I seen. C, I saw.

68
00:04:16.483 --> 00:04:18.413
The answer is B: have I seen.

69
00:04:19.917 --> 00:04:21.626
Rarely blank late for training.

70
00:04:21.926 --> 00:04:24.871
A, he is. B, is he. C, he was.

71
00:04:28.883 --> 00:04:30.523
The answer is B: is he.

72
00:04:32.017 --> 00:04:34.759
The best result ever achieved in the world is a blank.

73
00:04:35.059 --> 00:04:38.643
A, world record. B, fan culture. C, match-fixing.

74
00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.475
The answer is A: world record.

75
00:04:45.983 --> 00:04:48.819
According to the text, what is attracting young audiences?

76
00:04:49.119 --> 00:04:53.945
A, doping. B, esports and new fan culture. C, sponsorship.

77
00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.913
The answer is B: esports and new fan culture.

78
00:05:02.417 --> 00:05:06.195
Now it's your turn to speak. Should esports be considered a real sport?

79
00:05:11.495 --> 00:05:18.046
Not only does esports need skill and teamwork, but it also has millions of fans, so I think it should.

80
00:05:18.346 --> 00:05:19.881
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:20.883 --> 00:05:25.486
Great work today! You learned eight new words and inversion after negative adverbials.

82
00:05:25.786 --> 00:05:29.565
Today's value is fair play. Play fairly and follow the rules.

83
00:05:29.865 --> 00:05:32.238
